菲尔
Aw, Phil.

587
00:18:08,740 --> 00:18:10,040
你最好了
You're the best.

588
00:18:12,080 --> 00:18:14,220
没有谁像你这样
There's no one like you.

589
00:18:23,780 --> 00:18:25,060
克莱尔 看起来真好吃
Claire, that looks so good.

590
00:18:25,100 --> 00:18:26,400
我等不及要尝尝了
I can't wait to try it.

591
00:18:26,460 --> 00:18:27,480
谢谢
Thank you.

592
00:18:31,380 --> 00:18:32,880
有什么地方不太对劲
Something has happened here.

593
00:18:35,340 --> 00:18:36,740
你们一定很高兴
Well, you'll all be happy to know

594
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:38,180
我们为了找到蛋糕装饰人偶
that our search for the cake topper

595
00:18:38,180 --> 00:18:40,180
挖出了好多家族宝贝
unearthed a number of family treasures.

596
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:41,920
拜托 小卡 我们这正吃饭呢
Come on, Cam. We're eating over here.

597
00:18:42,140 --> 00:18:42,540
等一下
Wait.

598
00:18:42,540 --> 00:18:44,640
这不是父亲节我送给你的吗
Didn't I give you this for Father's Day?

599
00:18:45,160 --> 00:18:45,700
还有这个
And that.

600
00:18:45,940 --> 00:18:47,020
看到这狗的本性了吧
You see how this dog is?

601
00:18:47,900 --> 00:18:49,760
我的卡拉OK麦克风
My karaoke microphone.

602
00:18:49,900 --> 00:18:50,840
杰 快看
Jay, check it out!

603
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:52,749
是另一个无线通话机
The other walkie-talkie!

604
00:18:52,759 --> 00:18:54,000
真替你脸红 杰·普里契特
Shame on you, Jay Pritchett!

605
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,780
你利用这只狗把你讨厌的东西都埋了
You have used this dog to bury the things that you hate.

606
00:18:56,780 --> 00:18:57,409
-什么 -没错
- What? - Yeah!

607
00:18:57,409 --> 00:18:59,200
你从何时开始需要别人帮你埋东西了
Since when do you need help burying things?

608
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:01,360
淡定 她也埋了我的东西 看
Calm down. She buries stuff of mine, too. Look.

609
00:19:02,220 --> 00:19:04,780
上个月办公室的人给我买了这只钟
Everybody at the office bought me this clock last month.

610
00:19:05,100 --> 00:19:06,380
宝贝 你是怎么回事
Honey, what's the matter with you?

611
00:19:06,380 --> 00:19:07,319
这个问题该问你吧
That's a question that maybe you should answer.

612
00:19:07,319 --> 00:19:08,127
天呐 我的耳机
Oh, my gosh! My headphones!

613
00:19:08,138 --> 00:19:09,754
这太恶劣了
That's the worst.

614
00:19:11,723 --> 00:19:13,663
谨以此庆祝从业40周年
"Here's to 40 years in the business.

615
00:19:13,663 --> 00:19:16,723
享受你的新家伙吧 老家伙
Enjoy your new timer, old-timer."

616
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:19,960
我猛然间明白了
Suddenly, it made sense.

617
00:19:20,040 --> 00:19:21,080
在我爸爸眼里
In my dad's mind,

618
00:19:21,120 --> 00:19:23,500
我要接住火炬了 而他还不想传下去
I was reaching for a torch he wasn't ready to pass.

619
00:19:23,660 --> 00:19:24,660
确实有朝一日
Sure, someday,

620
00:19:24,660 --> 00:19:25,800
我会接手他的生意
I'm gonna take over his business,

621
